      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Moiré engineering created a tunable platform for correlated quantum matter and revealed unexpected superconducting and insulating phases, opening a major new direction in condensed-matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Bistritzer and MacDonald supplied the key theoretical prediction of flat bands; Jarillo-Herrero led the experiments that established the correlated phases.",
        "maturity": "The phenomenon has attracted broad experimental and theoretical scrutiny, though the field's understanding of the phases continues to develop.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The mechanisms behind superconductivity and the relation among observed phases remain unsettled.",
          "Credit for the broader moiré field extends beyond these foundational contributions."
        ]
      }
    },
