        "Corey S. O'Hern",
        "Sidney R. Nagel"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Work on jamming and rigidity gave disordered matter a powerful framework for understanding how mechanical stability emerges, with connections to granular materials, glasses, and soft matter.",
        "attribution": "Liu, O'Hern, and Nagel made central theoretical and experimental contributions to defining and testing the transition.",
        "maturity": "The framework has generated extensive research, but its relation to different forms of glassy arrest and its general limits remain active questions.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The transition's status as a sharply defined universal phenomenon across different systems is not fully settled.",
          "The discovery and its credit are distributed across a broad community."
        ]
      }
